      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The prevalence of asthma continues to grow rapidly among children in areas undergoing urbanization. Current pharmacotherapy for asthma reduces inflammation and provides symptomatic relief, but it does not work for all patients and it does not entirely suppress the underlying disease. For these reasons new therapeutic approaches are still needed. Anti-IgE, the newest therapeutic modality for asthma, a biologic agent to control allergic disorders, represents a fundamentally new concept in treatment."},
